{
  "title": "Samyama Graph — overview",
  "uid": "samyama-overview",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": true,
  "time": { "from": "now-6h", "to": "now" },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "tags": ["samyama", "graph"],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "job",
        "label": "Job",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
        "query": "label_values(samyama_nodes, job)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this shows, and what it does not",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Every panel reads a metric `/metrics` actually exports — there is no panel here for a metric that does not exist, because a dashboard with empty panels teaches an operator to ignore it.\n\n**Not here, because it is not exported:** per-query-shape latency, rows scanned, plan choice. To find *which* query is slow, read the slow-query log (`SLOW_QUERY_MS`), which carries the query text; the `samyama_slow_queries_total` panel below tells you when to go and look. Tracing is not shipped."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Query latency percentiles",
      "description": "From the latency histogram. A mean would hide exactly the case that matters: one query in twenty over budget moves a mean by nothing.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 5 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "s" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(samyama_query_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(samyama_query_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(samyama_query_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queries per second, and how many failed",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 5 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(samyama_queries_total{job=\"$job\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "executed"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(samyama_queries_failed_total{job=\"$job\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "failed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Slow queries — go and read the log",
      "description": "Past SLOW_QUERY_MS, the same threshold the slow-query log uses, so this panel and that log never disagree about what counts as slow.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 13 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(samyama_slow_queries_total{job=\"$job\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "slow/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency band occupancy",
      "description": "Where queries land, as a share. A shift from the sub-millisecond bands into the 100 ms band is visible here before any percentile crosses an alert threshold.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 13 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (le) (rate(samyama_query_duration_seconds_bucket{job=\"$job\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "<= {{le}}s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Graph size",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 20 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "samyama_nodes{job=\"$job\"}", "legendFormat": "nodes" },
        { "expr": "samyama_edges{job=\"$job\"}", "legendFormat": "edges" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Memory attributed",
      "description": "samyama_memory_attributed_bytes is what the engine can account for, not RSS. A gap between the two is unattributed memory and is worth an issue.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 8, "x": 8, "y": 20 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "bytes" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "samyama_memory_attributed_bytes{job=\"$job\"}", "legendFormat": "attributed" },
        { "expr": "samyama_index_memory_bytes{job=\"$job\"}", "legendFormat": "indexes" },
        { "expr": "sum by (label, property) (samyama_index_bytes{job=\"$job\"})", "legendFormat": "{{label}}.{{property}}" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "AST cache hit ratio",
      "description": "A ratio, not two counters: the absolute numbers grow without bound and say nothing on their own.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 8, "x": 16, "y": 20 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "percentunit", "max": 1, "min": 0 }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(samyama_query_cache_hits{job=\"$job\"}[5m]) / clamp_min(rate(samyama_query_cache_hits{job=\"$job\"}[5m]) + rate(samyama_query_cache_misses{job=\"$job\"}[5m]), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "hit ratio"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "__inputs": [
    {
      "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
      "label": "Prometheus",
      "type": "datasource",
      "pluginId": "prometheus"
    }
  ]
}
